{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I heard a [C]voice from the [G]throne
Look, God's [D]dwelling is with [Em]us
[C]He will dwell with his [G]own
And they will be his [D]people
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He will [C]wipe away every [G]tear
From our [D]eyes up [Em]there
[C]And death will be no [G]more
No more [D]grief or crying or [G]pain
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When [C]I walk my final [G]road
And [D]my journey here is [Em]done
[C]Then I will see him as he [G]is
And be at home with [D]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He will [C]wipe away every [G]tear
From our [D]eyes up [Em]there
And [C]death will be no [G]more
